{"name": "Elkanth Aspirant", "type": "race", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Personal Branch</p><p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Elkanth</p><p>This branch represents the vast majority of elkanths. There are no additional physical descriptors associated with it beyond what is described in the core race, but what it does represent is the latent potential for metamorphosis.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Elkanth Aspirant Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Branching Aspects:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.Q78C6Z5AKLUHOP26]{Branching Aspects}</li><li><strong>Sprouting Aptitude:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.IZYXPF83UQ61P6EH]{Sprouting Aptitude}</li><li><strong>Metamorphosis:</strong> At 5th level, your body is permanently transformed as you take on a morph, one of the distinct forms present among your kind. Choose either the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.R66ZDNJYPDYIN1NS]{Mystic Morph}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.JUXEYSN2P7EZD3C6]{Herald Morph}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.XQIU5OOB7L0LLU45]{Knight Morph}, or @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.RW3NZGJT6FY8E162]{Spectra Morph} and gain all of its abilities. Additionally, you lose the <strong>Branching Aspects</strong> ability and any attribute increases gained from it.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "GO559C2BD1L6JBTD", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elkanth Echo", "type": "race", "img": "icons/commodities/treasure/figurine-elk.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Personal Branch</p><p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Elkanth</p><p>Not every elkanth that emerges from the ground is a blank slate, it would seem. In some unusual cases, an elkanth may be hatched with fragments of memory that are not their own. It is said that these memories originate from a past life, the last vestiges still clutched by a soul that even in rebirth could not let go. Many of the elkanth who find themselves possessed of such mementos are drawn to travel the wider world, searching for answers to the burning questions these misplaced memories raise. Those who are able to fully connect with these lost echoes can even begin to display physical aspects reminiscent of who they once were, lending them their own unique kind of metamorphosis.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Elkanth Echo Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Familiar Aspects.</strong> Three different attributes of your choice increase by 1. This bonus will be replaced at 5th level, so make a note of which attributes you chose.</li><li><strong>Echoes of a Past Life.</strong> Choose one branch from a different race to represent yourself in a past life. This choice affects the other abilities granted by this branch race.</li><li><strong>Echoed Words.</strong> You learn one language of your choice, remembered from your past life.</li><li><strong>Echoed Deeds.</strong> You gain proficiency with one skill and one trade of your choice, reflecting something you excelled at in your past life.</li><li><strong>Echo Metamorphosis.</strong> At 5th level, your body is permanently transformed as you take on a morph, one of the distinct forms present among your kind. You gain all of the abilities of the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.YRLU5DY2C4QOIY0B]{Echo Morph}. Additionally, you lose the <strong>Familiar Aspects</strong> ability and any attribute increases gained from it.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "UGLE1CR752DCKC4F", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Chthonic Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Chthonic Lep'ix have an affinity for the realms of gloom and turmoil. Their mystical gifts portend ruin and obscuration. Wing patterns may include features such as uncanny visages, chaotic intersecting geometry, or sinister eyes, to name a few.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Chthonic Lep'ix Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Dexterity and Presence both increase by 1.</li><li><b>Chthonic Magic: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.T8FJEIROS5Z5B8TH]{Chthonic Magic}</li><li><b>Baleful Resistance: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.U2LZOAWTN9HEYR6F]{Baleful Resistance}</li><li><b>Darkvision 60ft: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.1F3VSNLQTVMYA4PE]{Darkvision 60ft}</li><li><b>Ominous Sight: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.G0FGCDYBZHCRKAO7]{Ominous Sight}</li><li><b>Cryptic Essence: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.LH7JHOI6Q9N5ES88]{Cryptic Essence}</li><li><b>Language: </b>You can speak, read, and write Infernal.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "RNRG6C64OJFIX4EK", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Elysian Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Elysian Lep'ix have an affinity for the realms of idyll and divine grace. Their mystical gifts harken to the splendor and providence of an ideal world. Wing patterns may include features such as breath-taking butterfly colors, stained glass-like collages, or mimicked embossment of precious metals, to name a few.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Elysian Lep'ix Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Presence and Wisdom both increase by 1.</li><li><b>Elysian Magic: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.4VJ2G7YQ1FMRJWEX]{Elysian Magic}</li><li><b>Omen of Fortune: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.WSK3MYKHHGFSAXNM]{Omen of Fortune}</li><li><b>Empyrean Resistance: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.0Z0Q6FNI3460D9OW]{Empyrean Resistance}</li><li><b>Healing Hands: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.AHPJ6C17ALZ9WJ8G]{Healing Hands}</li><li><b>Language: </b>You can speak, read, and write Celestial.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "3742KSRAIK74QZTT", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Sidereal Lep'ix", "type": "race", "img": "icons/environment/creatures/bug-tick-red.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Sidereal Lep'ix have an affinity for the realms of the stars and the celestial bodies. Their mystical gifts are reminiscent of the grandeur of a starlit night and the pull of planets and moons as they dance above us. Wing patterns may include features such as glittering constellations, colorful nebulas, or concentric and intersecting ellipses, to name a few.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Sidereal Lep'ix Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Insectoid</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Intelligence and Wisdom both increase by 1.</li><li><b>Sidereal Magic: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.SZB7LUSQ2DP1Z38K]{Sidereal Magic}</li><li><b>Twilight Messenger: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.5VBCE0TI5ROEEH8N]{Twilight Messenger}</li><li><b>Gravitational Interference: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ATC9IW4AOMA74635]{Gravitational Interference}</li><li><b>Languages: </b>You can speak, read, and write Farspeak.</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "QMMAJJDWRFK1TZ3C", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Hydrothermal Mandrid", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Hydrothermal Mandrids most closely resemble fire salamanders, though perhaps taken to a new extreme. These Mandrid are adapted to thrive amongst the volcanic vents in the ocean's depths and have an innate affinity for the extreme heat and chill found there. Their bodies have the color and smoothness of cooled lava, with bright spots of red, orange, or yellow that are warm to the touch and slowly shift in hue, shape, and position in a manner reminiscent of a lava lamp. When a Hydrothermal Mandrid channels magics that are fiery or chilling in nature, the intensity of color and motion for these vibrant spots will increase or decrease in response as the thermal repercussions of these elemental energies reverberate through its body.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Hydrothermal Mandrid Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Aquatic</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Intelligence, Wisdom, or Presence score increases by 1.</li><li><b>Extremophile: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ZSFV2WOU1HUP17KZ]{Extremophile}</li><li><b>Deep Ocean Adaptation: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.Z8LMDPJW67U417SF]{Deep Ocean Adaptation}</li><li><b>Heat Transfer: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.LSXJQMNO1E738IQC]{Heat Transfer}</li><li><b>Elemental Equilibrium: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.614UPFMARNM1ROVC]{Elemental Equilibrium}</li><li><b>Darkvision 30ft: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.K2R4176S4B99TO6R]{Darkvision 30ft}</li><li><b>Sunlight Sensitivity: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.0YK75ZQYDRVHEP50]{Sunlight Sensitivity}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "PP9LCJTN1A4RY8Q3", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Resolute Mandrid", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Resolute Mandrids most closely resemble axolotls, with colorful, frilly external gills and a long tadpole-like fin framing their tail. Their skin comes in a variety of pastel colors, which combined with their other charming features make them generally viewed as the most approachable Mandrids. They get their namesake from their seemingly miraculous ability to shrug off any injury short of death, given enough time to rest.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Resolute Mandrid Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Aquatic</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Constitution or Presence score increases by 1.</li><li><b>Natural Regeneration: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.NZF69C583MKEQ0PB]{Natural Regeneration}</li><li><b>Fearless: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.NG4N84ST7ES1J9IE]{Fearless}</li><li><b>Fascinating Colors: </b>@Compendium[undertaking.abilities.ZNZV2MPB10KLX45B]{Fascinating Colors}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "4CQR3D77S691MAUS", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Toxic Mandrid", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-shark-swimming.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Toxic Mandrids' appearance can vary significantly, but they always sport bright warning color patterns on their skin, a warning of the toxins stored within. They are well adapted to living in lakes, swamps, and jungles - just about anywhere with ample moisture will do, as their latent toxins tend to make would-be predators think twice.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Toxic Mandrid Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Aquatic</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Constitution score increases by 1.</li><li><b>Sluggish Step: </b>Your walking and swim speed both decrease by 5 feet.</li><li><b>Resist Toxins: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.2PRN9S8X7YFBJP10]{Resist Toxins}</li><li><b>Crushing Bite: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.XTBTJVESG8QZXIDM]{Crushing Bite}</li><li><b>Inject Venom: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.PT5XC6EU86D58ODI]{Inject Venom}</li><li><b>Secrete Toxin: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.EZ51QFJQ8CC1P3GQ]{Secrete Toxin}</li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AYPE0HZ9W2EQYW0Q", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Frost-Hide Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Cultural Branch</p><p><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</p><p>The Frost-Hide minotaurs are well adapted to life in the harsh, snowy wastes. Their fur hide is thicker and comes in shades of whites and grays.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "branch", "classDetails": "<p>Frost-Hide Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Attribute Increase:</strong> Your Constitution score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Cold Resistance:</strong> You have resistance to cold damage.</li><li><strong>Frost Walker:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.7AJZXIVS9CA03LF9]{Frost Walker}</li><li><strong>Tundra Heart: </strong>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.EYQFU3YGB3FQ3GXE]{Tundra Heart}</li><li><strong><em>Alternate Heritage:</em></strong> Minotaur heritage can present in various ways. If your core race does not grant you Horns, you can choose to replace either the &ldquo;Cold Resistance&rdquo; or &ldquo;Tundra Heart&rdquo; trait offered by this branch race with the following ability:<ul><li><strong>Lesser Horns:</strong> You have horns, which function as a natural weapon that deals piercing damage equal to 1d4 plus your Strength modifier on a hit. You are proficient with your horns, but they do not grant any extra attacks, actions, or minor actions on their own.</li></ul></li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "AYBMCPON8HWMAUYQ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Mountain-Horn Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The Mountain-Horn minotaurs thrive in some of the most rugged environments. Steep terrain has honed their strength, and their horns have become fortified through contests with the local predators, giving these minotaurs their iconic name.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Mountain-Horn Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><strong>Compatibility: </strong>Bestial</li><li><strong>Attribute Increase: </strong>Your Strength score increases by 1.</li><li><strong>Heavy Hitter: </strong>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.666YST9UQN7QPICB]{Heavy Hitter}</li><li><strong>Weapon Proficiency: </strong>You gain proficiency with Greatclubs, Greataxes, and Warhammers.</li><li><strong><em>Alternate Heritage:</em></strong> Minotaur heritage can present in various ways. If your core race does not grant you Horns, you can choose to replace the &ldquo;Weapon Proficiency&rdquo; trait offered by this branch race with the following ability:<ul><li><strong>Lesser Horns:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.MPBFI0K1205Z8O2G]{Lesser Horns}</li></ul></li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "EGXEOQWFJLSJ1M3T", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Valley-Hoof Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The Valley-Hoof minotaurs are most often found amid rolling hills and fertile valleys. Their stout build makes tough work like mining, hauling, and smithing look easy, and the abundance these boons bring make for a hale constitution.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Valley-Hoof Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Bestial</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Constitution score increases by 1.</li><li><b>Toughness: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.WNJ59P887AGGA1ZA]{Toughness}</li><li><b>Mighty Physique: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.WZKVGY28MAZHGYMK]{Mighty Physique}</li><li><strong><em>Alternate Heritage:</em></strong> Minotaur heritage can present in various ways. If your core race does not grant you Horns, you can choose to replace the @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.WZKVGY28MAZHGYMK]{Mighty Physique} trait offered by this branch race with the following ability:<ul><li><strong>Lesser Horns:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.MPBFI0K1205Z8O2G]{Lesser Horns}</li></ul></li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "7R4JLL591XQVOKK8", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Wild-Blood Minotaur", "type": "race", "img": "icons/creatures/abilities/paw-print-tan.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>The Wild-Blood minotaurs share a kinship with the more primeval and remote stretches of the wilderness. They sport shorter horns and longer fur than most of their kin. Their tie to the natural energies of the world is rather unique, and it's quite common to see a lesser natural spirit in animal form striding beside a Wild-Blood minotaur.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "portion": "core", "classDetails": "<p>Wild-Blood Minotaur Traits</p><ul><li><b>Compatibility: </b>Bestial</li><li><b>Attribute Increase: </b>Your Wisdom score increases by 1.</li><li><b>Wild Spirit: </b>@Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.7U9PFUNYXKJE4423]{Wild Spirit}</li><li><b>Favor of the Land: </b>You gain proficiency in one of the following: Intelligence (Nature), Botany, Fishing, or Pathfinding Trade.</li><li><strong><em>Alternate Heritage:</em></strong> Minotaur heritage can present in various ways. If your core race does not grant you Horns, you can choose to replace the &ldquo;Favor of the Land&rdquo; trait offered by this branch race with the following ability:<ul><li><strong>Lesser Horns:</strong> @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.MPBFI0K1205Z8O2G]{Lesser Horns}</li></ul></li></ul>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "S15CACVO0VP809K2", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
